#x02013;34.4</td><td align="left">27.2&#x02013;38.5</td><td align="left">32.6&#x02013;39.2</td><td align="left">22.4&#x02013;24.0</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>a </sup>Amino acid sequences corresponding to AQP1 (bovine), GlpF (<italic>E. coli</italic>) and AqpZ (<italic>E. coli</italic>) were used for this analysis. The corresponding PDB codes of these proteins are <ext-link ext-link-type="pdb" xlink:href="1J4N">1J4N</ext-link>, <ext-link ext-link-type="pdb" xlink:href="1FX8">1FX8</ext-link> and <ext-link ext-link-type="pdb" xlink:href="1RC2">1RC2</ext-link> and they served as template structures for the plant MIP modeling.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>